ck army ready for the northern Wei campaign; 5,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Fan Yi, at Qin Capital Basin, task: maintain the Qin mobile reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign; 3,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Shou Hei Kun, at Qin Eastern Military Depot, task: maintain the eastern reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign. Combined Qin strength on the current campaign roster is 176,800. The staff designate Sanyou as the present operational area. Qin has authorized movement into the target state; the field command may now advance toward Sanyou. Intelligence estimate: an official estimate of roughly 94,000-156,000 troops able to influence the theater; reported opposing commanders: Deng Shan, Gai Mou, Go Hou Mei, Huan Zhen, Jing Ning, Jing Rong, Luo Qian, Qiao He, Qiao Jie, Rei Ou; no confirmed battle contact. These are staff estimates rather than confirmed enemy counts. The Bureau's written orders direct the field command to concentrate and report at Kanyou, then march toward Sanyou when Tang Wei gives the order.","claim_status":"runtime_established_estimate","classification":"command_intelligence","confidence":"0.800","confidence_milli":800,"created_at":"244-BCE-09-29T19:00:00+08:00","deliveries":[],"discoverability_milli":1000,"epistemic_kind":"official_military_briefing","evidence_refs":["operation_arc_131572c4e8a2892bbc"],"fact":"Qin Military Bureau briefing. Tang Wei's field command numbers 9,500 troops in 19 formation(s), currently at Sanyou. Of these, 5,000 are Qin-assigned troops and 4,500 are House or retinue troops accompanying under Tang Wei's own authority. Other Qin forces on the campaign roster: 73,200 troops in 3 formation(s), under Kanki, Mou Gou, Ousen, at Qin Capital Basin, Qin Northern Frontier, task: concentrate Mou Gou, Ousen, and Kanki field forces for the northern Wei campaign; 46,100 troops in 2 formation(s), under Ouki, Tou, at Qin Eastern March, task: concentrate Ouki and Tou field forces for the northern Wei campaign; 40,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Mou Bu, at Qin Southern March, task: hold Mou Bu's shock army ready for the northern Wei campaign; 5,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Fan Yi, at Qin Capital Basin, task: maintain the Qin mobile reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign; 3,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Shou Hei Kun, at Qin Eastern Military Depot, task: maintain the eastern reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign. Combined Qin strength on the current campaign roster is 176,800. The staff designate Sanyou as the present operational area. Qin has authorized movement into the target state; the field command may now advance toward Sanyou. Intelligence estimate: an official estimate of roughly 94,000-156,000 troops able to influence the theater; reported opposing commanders: Deng Shan, Gai Mou, Go Hou Mei, Huan Zhen, Jing Ning, Jing Rong, Luo Qian, Qiao He, Qiao Jie, Rei Ou; no confirmed battle contact. These are staff estimates rather than confirmed enemy counts. The Bureau's written orders direct the field command to concentrate and report at Kanyou, then march toward Sanyou when Tang Wei gives the order.","holder_states":{"char_tang_wei":{"channel":"Qin Military Bureau operational briefing","confidence_milli":800,"epistemic_kind":"official_military_briefing","learned_at":"244-BCE-09-29T19:00:00+08:00","source_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign"}},"information_ref":"information.qin_campaign_briefing.7d2508aafa2902526082","investigation_discoverable":false,"knowers":["char_tang_wei"],"location_ref":"loc_sanyou","origin_authority":"runtime_established","owner_id":"information.qin_campaign_briefing.7d2508aafa2902526082","provenance":"Qin Military Bureau operational briefing","schema":"sword-information","subject_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign","world_truth_authority":false}
